# Known DICOM viewing limitations

## Interactive viewer

The viewer preserves access to the originals for these objects, which lack
a dedicated preview:

- Philips private CT transfer syntax
- Philips HP Live 3D 02
- Raw Data Storage
- RT Structure Set Storage
- Enhanced US Volume Storage

Grayscale presentation states can apply supported windows, crop, orientation
and annotations. Sampled Presentation LUTs in a presentation state remain
unsupported. Sampled grayscale VOI LUTs in images are supported.

Surface Segmentation previews need WebGL. Facets with more than three points
are unsupported. See [supported formats](docs/GUIDE.md#image-support).

## PDF reference images

The converter preserves files using the private GE 3D layout, HTJ2K images,
Parametric Maps and Surface Segmentation without rendering them as PDF reference
images. The interactive viewer can display HTJ2K images, supported Parametric Maps
and supported Surface Segmentation meshes.

## Input errors and recovery

Invalid pixel bit layouts, inconsistent RT Dose frame counts, missing required
file-meta information and truncated data can prevent display. Check the selected
file's metadata and any diagnostic PDF page for details.

Choose **Save → Original file**, or use the download button next to the entry
under **Metadata → Other supplied files**. The CLI also supports `extract`.
See the [format matrix](docs/GUIDE.md#image-support) and
[recovery instructions](docs/GUIDE.md#save-original-files).
